That's simply false. My wizards typically hit Mines
Town dressed like tanks to help them survive having
low HPs, buy protection, then discard their metal
body armor so that they can start upgrading their
spellcasting skills. Lots and lots of times I'm
throwing away +2 dwarven mithral that has outlived
its usefulness, dumping dwarven roundshields with no
intention of ever again wearing a shield, losing
metal helms to wear none, or, if lucky, a leather
one. I mostly keep footwear, which doesn't seem to
affect spellcasting so much.

> Which leaves lowered AC. Frankly, I find the claim
> of "9 to 20 points" rather humorous; certainly the
> higher numbers are more theoretical than real. If
> you manage to get enough money for donations to
> get into the high teens of protection while still
